{"body":"## Why\n\nThis stack has been running in production (the gas-station fleet) since late June via locally-built binaries (v1.1.0-rc.1 line), but never landed on main. That divergence is now biting: the fleet's Dolt DBs were migrated to **schema v54** by those binaries, so a main-built `bd` (v53) half-fails against them — reads mostly work, but e.g. `bd export --all` errors, which silently truncated a git-tracked memories backup to 0 bytes tonight before being caught. Main must catch up to the schema its own deployments already created.\n\n## What\n\nLands `origin/feat/lease-primitive` into main, plus one finished commit stranded on a local checkout:\n\n- `fix(dolt)`: retry mutate+commit methods on serialization conflict (1213/1205)\n- `test(dolt)`: concurrent work-queue drain test (gas-station claim invariant)\n- `feat(lease)`: claim-TTL + heartbeat + reclaim for dead-worker recovery — **includes migration `0054_add_lease_columns`**\n- ci: allowlist lease stress tests / TestConcurrentWorkQueueDrain for the testing.Short() policy\n- `feat(show)`: surface lease_expires_at/heartbeat_at in `bd show` (--json + text) (wy-9cdw) — cherry-picked from the local `~/beads` checkout where it was stranded\n- merge of origin/main (clean auto-merge, no conflicts)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` green\n- `go test ./internal/storage/schema/... ./cmd/bd -run 'TestEmbeddedMemory|Test.*Lease|Test.*Migrat'` green\n- Migration 0054 present (up+down)\n\n## Related\n\n- The `bd remember` desire-path fix (bare existing key recalls; bare unknown slug refused) is already on main @ 9ee97c264.\n- Branch `pave/remember-reads-rc1` (rc-line backport powering the currently installed binary) becomes redundant once this merges — delete it after the next release build.\n- After merge: the beads repo's own tracker DB (v51) needs its designated-migrator run (`BD_ALLOW_REMOTE_MIGRATE=1 bd migrate && bd dolt push`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOQAyAEs8AAAABIdOfjQ","author":{"login":"steveyegge"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## ⚠️ Post-merge / release checklist (do not skip)\n\n- [ ] **Migrate the beads repo's own tracker** (it's at v51, gated): `BD_ALLOW_REMOTE_MIGRATE=1 bd migrate && bd dolt push` — run on the ONE designated migrator machine (this laptop is fine); every other clone then `bd bootstrap`.\n- [ ] **Delete branch `pave/remember-reads-rc1`** — redundant once main-built binaries know v54 (its two commits are already on main).\n- [ ] **Rebuild + reinstall `bd` from main** on the laptop (replaces the rc1-line binary at `~/.local/bin/bd`; backup at `~/.local/bin/bd.pre-remember-fix.bak` can go too).\n- [ ] Also tracked as a bead in the wyvern DB (`bd list | grep -i 'beads release'`).","createdAt":"2026-07-02T05:26:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/4537#issuecomment-4862484365","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOQAyAEs8AAAABItayRA","author":{"login":"maphew"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Recommendation: hold it for the next release, don't jam it into 1.1.0 (which I'm trying to land today).\r\n\r\nCut v1.1.0 stable lean from the current v53 line (once #4566's recovery lands) to unblock everyone stuck on the gated 1.0.5. Then land #4537 on main after the tag, so v54 rides v1.2.0 with its own RC soak. Reasoning:\r\n- v1.1.0 has been in RC purgatory because of migration churn (#4502/#4534/#4555/#4566). Adding a 5th schema jump + 1600 lines of new surface right before the stable tag re-opens exactly that risk.\r\n- It's additive feature value, not a 1.1.0 blocker or a fix.\r\n- The fleet problem is solved by merging to main — decoupled from the 1.1.0 tag.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T21:41:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/4537#issuecomment-4879462980","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-06-25T19:21:11Z","authors":[{"email":"steve.yegge@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc0NA==","login":"steveyegge","name":"Steve Yegge"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-04T05:36:02Z","messageBody":"…3/1205)\n\nClaimIssue, ClaimReadyIssue, UpdateIssue and CloseIssue each hand-rolled\ntheir own tx (BeginTx + DOLT_ADD/DOLT_COMMIT + Commit) outside\nwithRetryTx, so a concurrent writer that lost Dolt's optimistic\ncommit-time merge surfaced MySQL 1213/1205 as a hard failure instead of\nretrying. Dolt has no real row locking — FOR UPDATE / SKIP LOCKED are\nparse-only no-ops (https://www.dolthub.com/blog/2023-10-23-hold-my-beer/)\n— so retry is the only safety net under N concurrent workers. These four\nare the work-queue hot paths: `bd ready --claim`, claim, update, close.\n\nMove each body into a withRetryTx closure (which owns BeginTx and the\nfinal Commit and retries serialization failures with backoff), preserving\nthe single-tx CAS/mutation + DOLT_COMMIT atomicity exactly. On retry,\nClaimReadyIssue re-scans the ready front from a fresh snapshot and claims\nthe next available issue.\n\nTested: TestEmbeddedReadyClaimConcurrent, TestEmbeddedReadyConcurrent,\nTestEmbeddedCloseConcurrent, TestEmbeddedUpdateConcurrent and the\nnon-concurrent embedded Update/Close/Ready tests pass; build + vet clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(dolt): retry mutate+commit methods on serialization conflict (121…","oid":"c017321249f53cfa090e9ba3b1b62baba8d8a0d6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-25T20:30:56Z","authors":[{"email":"steve.yegge@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc0NA==","login":"steveyegge","name":"Steve Yegge"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-04T05:36:02Z","messageBody":"…nvariant)\n\nN workers concurrently dequeue one shared ready-front via ClaimReadyIssue\nuntil empty; asserts every issue claimed exactly once, none stranded, no\ndouble-claims, and no serialization error ever surfaces (withRetryTx absorbs\nthe 1213/1205 from the claim-CAS cell collision). This is the regression guard\nfor the multi-agent claim queue that #4491 makes safe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"test(dolt): add concurrent work-queue drain test (Gas Station claim i…","oid":"6871220de1a9bc637011e9ed…6499 tokens truncated… (wy-x543k).\n\nNew verifiedClaimWrite resolves claim-family outcomes against the DB\ninstead of trusting exit status: reported success is verified by\nre-read and fails loudly on mismatch; an indeterminate commit-phase\nloss (errCommitPhase) is settled by re-read — applied becomes success,\nverified-rolled-back is replayed once. Wired into ClaimIssue,\nUnclaimIssue, UnclaimIssueIfAssignee, and ClaimReadyIssue (bespoke:\nclaimed ID only known post-body; a replay may legitimately claim a\ndifferent issue). Wisps and non-server mode exempt.\n\nMetrics: bd.claim_verify_lost_total, bd.claim_verify_recovered_total\n(op, outcome=applied|replayed).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(claim): verify claim-family writes by re-read under a degraded se…","oid":"a4b4b27da2f53d4bde7e13c371a9a55d2f267442"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-24T02:05:52Z","authors":[{"email":"steve.yegge@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc0NA==","login":"steveyegge","name":"Steve Yegge"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-24T02:05:52Z","messageBody":"Design handoff from wyvern's wheelhouse hostile-review (epic wy-mdi5h):\ngeneralize the claim-side CAS into --if-assignee/--if-status guards on\n'bd update', covering the X->Y reassign and status-guarded\nclaim-on-behalf transitions that --claim and unclaim --if-assignee\ncannot express. Authored by fly; committed so the untracked doc\nsurvives workspace cleanup. Depends on bd-zccb9 (verify-after-write).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(proposal): CAS conditional update design for bd-wsqvw (from fly)","oid":"a6b66026bd8a0a4d70a6f2d1a29c47b269c1a1bf"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-24T07:42:00Z","authors":[{"email":"steve.yegge@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc0NA==","login":"steveyegge","name":"Steve Yegge"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-24T07:42:00Z","messageBody":"…lion review)\n\nThe bespoke ClaimReadyIssue path's replay returned raw on any error, so a\nreplayed write dying at commit phase skipped the verify pass — reintroducing\nthe wy-x543k false-failure on attempt two, and potentially orphaning an\napplied claim on a DIFFERENT ready issue than the first attempt selected.\nThe replay now falls through to verify on errCommitPhase-with-selection,\nexactly like verifiedClaimWrite's leg: applied -> recovered success,\nverified rollback -> honest 'did not land' (budget already spent).\n\nExtracted the resolution loop as verifiedReadyClaim so injection tests can\ndrive the write seam; sixth test mirrors ConvertsAppliedIndeterminate on\nthe replay leg.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(claim): ready-claim replay leg keeps verify semantics (bd-zccb9, …","oid":"a03b33c9bc8713d485df5397599fd729ed36125b"}],"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","additions":19,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"PROPOSAL-cas-conditional-update.md","additions":167,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/claim_verify.go","additions":138,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/claim_verify_test.go","additions":244,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/issues.go","additions":146,"deletions":63,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/store.go","additions":19,"deletions":9,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"a45199a546f959044426b98716975c70b7c77a16"},"mergedAt":"2026-07-24T14:21:25Z","number":5006,"reviews":[],"state":"MERGED","title":"fix(claim): verify claim-family writes by re-read under a degraded server (bd-zccb9)"}

### 7
{"body":"## Summary\n\nImplements bd-wsqvw: general conditional (compare-and-set) update — `bd update --if-assignee <expected> [--if-status <expected>]`. Design: `PROPOSAL-cas-conditional-update.md` (fly's handoff from wyvern's wheelhouse hostile-review, epic wy-mdi5h), committed in the base PR #5006.\n\n**Stacked on #5006** (bd-zccb9 verify-after-write) — the guarded coordination writes route through its `verifiedClaimWrite`. Merge #5006 first; this PR's base is `bd-zccb9-claim-verify`.\n\nThe wheelhouse fleet's most common bug class is check-then-act on assignee/status: read state, decide, then issue a blind `bd update -a X` — and lose to a racing writer in the gap. Two transitions had no atomic primitive:\n\n- **Reassign X→Y** (park, wy-mdi5h.3): `bd update <id> --if-assignee worker -a mayor`\n- **Claim-on-behalf with a status guard** (restore, wy-mdi5h.6): `bd update <id> --if-assignee '' --if-status open -a owner -s in_progress`\n\nWhen a guard is present the mutation applies only if the current value still matches — one atomic transaction, nothing written on a mismatch, loud non-zero exit naming actual vs expected. `--if-assignee ''` is a real guard meaning \"expected unassigned\" (`Changed()`-detected, the unclaim idiom).\n\n## Design: reconciled with #4911\n\nThe proposal predates #4911 (`UpdateIssueChecked` + `ExpectedVersion` row CAS). Rather than the proposal's new `UpdateIssueIfMatch` interface method, the guards extend the **existing** `UpdateIssueOptions` (`ExpectedAssignee`/`ExpectedStatus` pointer fields, conjunction semantics, composing with `ExpectedVersion`):\n\n- No `Storage` interface break; decorators (`HookFiringStore`, `InstrumentedStorage`) pass through unchanged.\n- One shared guard primitive: `issueops.CheckExpectedFieldsInTx` beside `CheckVersionInTx`, typed `storage.ErrStatusMismatch` beside the existing `ErrAssigneeMismatch`.\n- Same two-limb atomicity as the version CAS (reviewed in #4911): the guard read shares the mutation's transaction, and a writer that commits mid-flight collides on the row_lock cell rewrite at commit time — the retry loop replays, re-reads the guard, and refuses.\n\nWired through **all three write stacks**: `DoltStore` (server mode, incl. the wisp and demote-to-wisp branches), `EmbeddedDoltStore`, and the proxied-server path (`domain.UpdateSpec` → `ApplyUpdate`, guard failures flowing through the finding-#10 non-zero exit contract).\n\n**bd-zccb9 integration:** in Dolt server mode a guarded update that writes assignee/status is claim-family — it resolves through `verifiedClaimWrite` with a `guardedUpdatePostcondition` (checks only the coordination fields the update actually sets), so its exit code stays truthful under a degraded server. Replay after a verified rollback re-checks the guards inside the replayed transaction, so a racing writer makes the replay refuse rather than clobber.\n\nCLI rules: guards are mutually exclusive with `--claim` (its own CAS with pool semantics), require a regular field update to ride on (label/parent edits run outside the guarded transaction), and `--if-status` is validated against the live status set so a typo fails fast instead of mismatching forever.\n\n## Testing\n\nAll against real engines; suites green:\n\n- `internal/storage/dolt/update_guards_test.go` (Dolt container): park reassign, atomic refuse (typed error, row untouched, no event), claim-on-behalf, `--if-assignee ''` semantics, guard conjunction, composition with `ExpectedVersion`, wisp routing, and `TestGuardedReassignConcurrent` — two racing guarded reassigns, exactly one winner, loser gets `ErrAssigneeMismatch`.\n- `internal/storage/embeddeddolt/update_guards_test.go`: same core through the embedded wrapper.\n- `cmd/bd/update_conditional_embedded_test.go` (CLI e2e): guarded transitions, exactly-once semantics, mismatch names actual state, flag-validation rejections write nothing.\n- `cmd/bd/update_conditional_proxied_test.go` (proxied server e2e): guarded reassign win/lose, claim-on-behalf, `--claim` exclusion.\n- Regressions: dolt + embedded `UpdateIssueChecked` version-CAS suites, claim-verify suite, `domain`, `issueops` — all pass. Build/vet/gofmt/golangci-lint clean.\n\nDocs note: per the 2026-07-17 docs-release-pin decision, no `docs/` changes — the generated CLI reference documents the pinned release; the flags are documented in `bd prime` output and CHANGELOG.\n\nThe wheelhouse *adoption* patches (queue-take wy-mdi5h.7, bulldog wy-mdi5h.4 switching to pool-aware `--claim`) are wyvern-side follow-ups, not part of this PR.\n\nCloses bd-wsqvw.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n**CI note:** the pr workflow triggers only on PRs targeting main (`pull_request: branches: [main]`), so checks appear on this PR when it retargets main after #5006 merges. All four local suite layers are green (details above). Main itself has a red Test Nix Flake from the #4942 go.mod bump — fix in #5009.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOQAyAEs8AAAABLgn1TA","author":{"login":"steveyegge"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Heads-up for review: one commit added since the branch was cut — 89dac6dc2 gives guard mismatches a distinct exit code so scripts can branch on the verdict (requested by fly, the wy-mdi5h designer, for the park/restore adopters).\n\nContract: exit **13** (`ExitGuardMismatch`) when every failed ID in the run was a stale `--if-assignee`/`--if-status` guard (a racer won — skip gracefully); exit 1 when any failure is anything else (infra — retry/abort). Both paths (direct + proxied) route through the same `updateIDFailure.GuardMismatch` plumbing; `--json` failure entries carry `\"guard_mismatch\": true`; stderr keeps the greppable `assignee mismatch`/`status mismatch` sentinels. Flag-validation errors stay exit 1 — 13 is reserved for real CAS refusals. Covered by new assertions in the embedded + proxied guard tests, incl. a mixed-batch-exits-1 case and a guard that exhausted-retry failures never masquerade as 13.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","createdAt":"2026-07-24T07:37:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/5008#issuecomment-5067371852","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOQAyAEs8AAAABLjN1pA","author":{"login":"steveyegge"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"## Review verdict (lion): APPROVE — merge after #5006 lands and this PR's CI runs green on the main retarget\n\nFull diff read (both commits, incl. 9c5ee07de's exit-13 contract). This is the right reconciliation of fly's proposal with #4911: guards as `UpdateIssueOptions` pointer fields (no interface break, decorators untouched), `CheckExpectedFieldsInTx` beside `CheckVersionInTx` with the same two-limb CAS argument (in-tx guard read refuses pre-committed writers; mid-flight writers collide on the row_lock rewrite and the retry re-checks), typed `ErrStatusMismatch` beside the existing assignee error, and `--if-assignee \"\"` as a real unassigned-guard via `Changed()`. Verified wired through all three stacks: DoltStore (incl. wisp route, demote-to-wisp sharing the demotion tx, and the verifiedClaimWrite integration), EmbeddedDoltStore, and the proxied `UpdateSpec`→`ApplyUpdate` path with the finding-#10 exit contract preserved. The CLI surface rules are right: `--claim` exclusion, field-update-to-ride-on requirement (label/parent edits genuinely run outside the guarded tx), up-front `--if-status` validation. `TestGuardedReassignConcurrent`'s exactly-one-winner against a real engine is the test that matters most, and it's here.\n\nThe exit-13 contract is well-shaped: 13 strictly for all-failures-were-stale-guards (\"racer won, don't retry\"), 1 for mixed/validation/infra, `guard_mismatch` in the JSON failure report, `ErrNotFound` correctly NOT a guard mismatch (conservative 1), and the proxied exhausted-conflicts test explicitly pins that conflict exhaustion never masquerades as 13. That's exactly the semantics wy-mdi5h.3/.6 scripts need to branch on.\n\n### Non-blocking notes\n\n1. **Document the verify postcondition's attribution narrowness.** `guardedUpdatePostcondition` checks only the coordination fields the update *sets*. Consider: guarded update `--if-assignee worker -a mayor --title X` hits a commit-phase loss and verifiably rolls back — while a racing actor lands the *same* reassign (worker→mayor). The re-read sees `assignee=mayor`, the wrapper reports recovered/applied success — but OUR transaction never landed: the title edit (and our event row) are silently gone despite exit 0. It needs commit-phase loss + a racer writing the same target value inside the verify window + extra fields riding the same update, so it's an edge-of-edge, and the coordination fields themselves ARE correct — but the doc comment currently only covers concurrent writers touching *other* fields. Add a sentence naming this case (and the mitigation: keep guarded coordination writes single-purpose, which is how both wheelhouse consumers use them). Not worth machinery to fix.\n2. Out-of-tree `Storage` implementations ignoring the new fields fail **open** (guards silently unenforced). The CHANGELOG names it, which is the right call given the no-interface-break choice — just flagging that I considered it.\n3. `updates[\"assignee\"].(string)` in `guardedUpdatePostcondition`: a library caller passing a non-string assignee value would skip verification while still writing. CLI can't produce this; fine as-is.\n\nSince the pr workflow only fires on main-targeted PRs, my approval is conditioned on the retargeted CI run being green — with 4 local layers already green I expect no drama. No re-review needed for the retarget itself or for a doc-comment addition per note 1.\n","createdAt":"2026-07-24T12:58:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/5008#issuecomment-5070091684","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-24T03:52:11Z","authors":[{"email":"steve.yegge@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc0NA==","login":"steveyegge","name":"Steve Yegge"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-24T14:22:26Z","messageBody":"…tatus (bd-wsqvw)\n\nFrom wyvern's wheelhouse hostile-review (epic wy-mdi5h): the fleet's most\ncommon bug class is check-then-act on bd assignee/status — read state,\nthen issue a blind 'bd update -a X', and lose to a racing writer in the\ngap. Design: PROPOSAL-cas-conditional-update.md.\n\nAdds --if-assignee/--if-status precondition flags to 'bd update'. When\npresent, the mutation applies only if the issue's current\nassignee/status still equals the expected value — one atomic\ntransaction, nothing written on a mismatch, loud non-zero exit naming\nactual vs expected. --if-assignee '' means \"expected unassigned\"\n(Changed()-detected, the unclaim idiom). Covers the two transitions no\nexisting verb expresses: reassign X->Y (park) and claim-on-behalf with\na status guard (restore).\n\nPer the reconciliation with #4911, the guards extend the existing\nUpdateIssueOptions on UpdateIssueChecked (ExpectedAssignee /\nExpectedStatus, new issueops.CheckExpectedFieldsInTx beside\nCheckVersionInTx, typed storage.ErrStatusMismatch beside the existing\nErrAssigneeMismatch) rather than minting a parallel interface method —\nno Storage interface break, decorators pass through unchanged. Wired\nthrough all three write stacks: DoltStore (server), EmbeddedDoltStore,\nand the proxied-server domain.UpdateSpec/ApplyUpdate path. In Dolt\nserver mode a guarded update that writes assignee/status is\nclaim-family and resolves through verifiedClaimWrite (bd-zccb9) with a\nguarded-update postcondition, so its exit code stays truthful under a\ndegraded server; replay after a verified rollback re-checks the guards\nin the replayed transaction.\n\nCLI rules: guards are mutually exclusive with --claim (its own CAS),\nrequire a regular field update to ride on (label/parent edits run\noutside the guarded transaction), and --if-status is validated against\nthe live status set so a typo fails fast instead of mismatching\nforever. Guard failures flow through the finding-#10 exit contract on\nboth the classic and proxied paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(update): conditional compare-and-set guards --if-assignee/--if-s…","oid":"d6800738fbfc6ff9435e47a68a74b9d0a24860f9"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-24T07:27:32Z","authors":[{"email":"steve.yegge@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc0NA==","login":"steveyegge","name":"Steve Yegge"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-24T14:22:26Z","messageBody":"…ard mismatch from infra failure (bd-wsqvw)\n\nA stale guard now exits ExitGuardMismatch (13) when every failure in the\nrun was a guard refusal — scripts can tell 'a racer won, skip gracefully'\nfrom 'server down, retry/abort' without parsing prose. Mixed batches keep\nthe conservative exit 1. JSON failure entries carry guard_mismatch:true;\nstderr keeps the greppable 'assignee mismatch'/'status mismatch' sentinels.\nRequested by fly (wyvern) for the wy-mdi5h.3/.6 park/restore adopters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(update): exit code 13 distinguishes --if-assignee/--if-status gu…","oid":"39611d182985f9782f4c86ab1f0637b7d1b01386"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-24T14:20:33Z","authors":[{"email":"steve.yegge@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc0NA==","login":"steveyegge","name":"Steve Yegge"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-24T14:22:26Z","messageBody":"…lion review note 1, PR #5008)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(claim): note guardedUpdatePostcondition attribution narrowness (…","oid":"2e93dd320640a16f126114b010c72b6e8a68a3ee"}],"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","additions":27,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"cmd/bd/prime.go","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"cmd/bd/update.go","additions":123,"deletions":11,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"cmd/bd/update_conditional_embedded_test.go","additions":184,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"cmd/bd/update_conditional_proxied_test.go","additions":106,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"cmd/bd/update_input.go","additions":30,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"cmd/bd/update_proxied_server.go","additions":40,"deletions":30,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"cmd/bd/update_proxied_server_test.go","additions":13,"deletions":10,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/claim_verify.go","additions":52,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/issues.go","additions":45,"deletions":24,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/update_guards_test.go","additions":222,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"internal/storage/dolt/wisps.go","additions":16,"deletions":11,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"internal/storage/domain/issue.go","additions":41,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"internal/storage/embeddeddolt/issues.go","additions":15,"deletions":9,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"internal/storage/embeddeddolt/update_guards_test.go","additions":91,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"internal/storage/issueops/update_cas.go","additions":53,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"internal/storage/storage.go","additions":21,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"6e8af8bf80e1fd74729d05182a90443289669031"},"mergedAt":"2026-07-24T16:11:16Z","number":5008,"reviews":[],"state":"MERGED","title":"feat(update): conditional compare-and-set guards --if-assignee/--if-status (bd-wsqvw)"}

